{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>ואכחיד</b> — It is the way of the shepherd to have under his hand subordinate shepherds, and these three who died in one month — perhaps he alludes to the High Priest, who is Joshua, and the priest anointed for war, and the deputy priest. Or Haggai, Zechariah, and Malachi died, and prophecy ceased, for the prophet is like a shepherd." "<b>ותקצר נפשי</b> — upon the flock, to deliver them." "<b>מלת בחלה בי</b> — it has no parallel, and its meaning is like קצרה נפל (my spirit grew short)." "<b>מלת ותקצר</b> — and the proof is the word וגם."], :book :zechariah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {2 "Ibn Ezra states the phrase ותאמר נפשי בחלה has no parallel construction; translated his gloss on בחלה literally without expanding his compressed argument."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Zecharia -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/zecharya"] ["1" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=25&perek=5&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:46:46.360152116Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}